4,dune_ridge,1,11.2,133.7\\nDR04,dune_ridge,2,11.2,148.5\\nDR04,dune_ridge,3,11.2,178.3\\nDR04,dune_ridge,4,11.2,101.9\\nDR05,dune_ridge,1,15.6,162.6\\nDR05,dune_ridge,2,15.6,195.2\\nDR05,dune_ridge,3,15.6,124.8\\nDR05,dune_ridge,4,15.6,151.4\\nDR06,dune_ridge,1,10.5,118.3\\nDR06,dune_ridge,2,10.5,143.9\\nDR06,dune_ridge,3,10.5,167.5\\nDR06,dune_ridge,4,10.5,109.7\\nDR07,dune_ridge,1,13.3,189.1\\nDR07,dune_ridge,2,13.3,132.4\\nDR07,dune_ridge,3,13.3,156.2\\nDR07,dune_ridge,4,13.3,171.8\\nDR08,dune_ridge,1,8.7,145.6\\nDR08,dune_ridge,2,8.7,182.3\\nDR08,dune_ridge,3,8.7,318.7\\nDR08,dune_ridge,4,8.7,402.5\\nDR09,dune_ridge,1,7.9,287.2\\nDR09,dune_ridge,2,7.9,511.4\\nDR09,dune_ridge,3,7.9,364.9\\nDR09,dune_ridge,4,7.9,275.1\\nDR10,dune_ridge,1,6.4,448.3\\nDR10,dune_ridge,2,6.4,603.7\\nDR10,dune_ridge,3,6.4,331.5\\nDR10,dune_ridge,4,6.4,296.8\\nBB01,back_barrier,1,18.2,121.5\\nBB01,back_barrier,2,18.2,164.2\\nBB01,back_barrier,3,18.2,108.6\\nBB01,back_barrier,4,18.2,192.3\\nBB02,back_barrier,1,16.7,137.8\\nBB02,back_barrier,2,16.7,159.4\\nBB02,back_barrier,3,16.7,183.1\\nBB02,back_barrier,4,16.7,115.7\\nBB03,back_barrier,1,19.4,172.9\\nBB03,back_barrier,2,19.4,146.3\\nBB03,back_barrier,3,19.4,198.5\\nBB03,back_barrier,4,19.4,127.2\\nBB04,back_barrier,1,17.1,154.4\\nBB04,back_barrier,2,17.1,131.8\\nBB04,back_barrier,3,17.1,176.6\\nBB04,back_barrier,4,17.1,163.1\\nBB05,back_barrier,1,15.9,149.7\\nBB05,back_barrier,2,15.9,168.2\\nBB05,back_barrier,3,15.9,122.5\\nBB05,back_barrier,4,15.9,389.3\\nBB06,back_barrier,1,14.6,158.6\\nBB06,back_barrier,2,14.6,526.1\\nBB06,back_barrier,3,14.6,342.8\\nBB06,back_barrier,4,14.6,471.4\\nBB07,back_barrier,1,12.8,308.2\\nBB07,back_barrier,2,12.8,655.9\\nBB07,back_barrier,3,12.8,283.4\\nBB07,back_barrier,4,12.8,417.6\\nBB08,back_barrier,1,11.5,359.1\\nBB08,back_barrier,2,11.5,494.7\\nBB08,back_barrier,3,11.5,321.3\\nBB08,back_barrier,4,11.5,276.5\\nBB09,back_barrier,1,13.7,433.8\\nBB09,back_barrier,2,13.7,512.2\\nBB09,back_barrier,3,13.7,298.6\\nBB09,back_barrier,4,13.7,367.9\\nBB10,back_barrier,1,10.9,281.4\\nBB10,back_barrier,2,10.9,455.3\\nBB10,back_barrier,3,10.9,394.7\\nBB10,back_barrier,4,10.9,329.2\\nTF01,tidal_flat,1,5.2,113.6\\nTF01,tidal_flat,2,5.2,147.1\\nTF01,tidal_flat,3,5.2,169.8\\nTF01,tidal_flat,4,5.2,102.4\\nTF02,tidal_flat,1,4.8,191.3\\nTF02,tidal_flat,2,4.8,126.7\\nTF02,tidal_flat,3,4.8,158.2\\nTF02,tidal_flat,4,4.8,134.9\\nTF03,tidal_flat,1,6.1,177.5\\nTF03,tidal_flat,2,6.1,143.2\\nTF03,tidal_flat,3,6.1,362.6\\nTF03,tidal_flat,4,6.1,488.1\\nTF04,tidal_flat,1,3.9,521.7\\nTF04,tidal_flat,2,3.9,347.3\\nTF04,tidal_flat,3,3.9,612.4\\nTF04,tidal_flat,4,3.9,289.8\\nTF05,tidal_flat,1,5.7,398.2\\nTF05,tidal_flat,2,5.7,443.6\\nTF05,tidal_flat,3,5.7,276.1\\nTF05,tidal_flat,4,5.7,531.5\\nTF06,tidal_flat,1,4.3,305.9\\nTF06,tidal_flat,2,4.3,467.4\\nTF06,tidal_flat,3,4.3,382.7\\nTF06,tidal_flat,4,4.3,294.3\\nTF07,tidal_flat,1,6.8,559.1\\nTF07,tidal_flat,2,6.8,321.8\\nTF07,tidal_flat,3,6.8,406.5\\nTF07,tidal_flat,4,6.8,278.2\\nTF08,tidal_flat,1,3.5,634.6\\nTF08,tidal_flat,2,3.5,287.9\\nTF08,tidal_flat,3,3.5,412.3\\nTF08,tidal_flat,4,3.5,349.7\\nTF09,tidal_flat,1,5.9,372.4\\nTF09,tidal_flat,2,5.9,508.1\\nTF09,tidal_flat,3,5.9,296.5\\nTF09,tidal_flat,4,5.9,441.8\\nTF10,tidal_flat,1,4.1,316.3\\nTF10,tidal_flat,2,4.1,479.6\\nTF10,tidal_flat,3,4.1,353.2\\nTF10,tidal_flat,4,4.1,588.4\\n\",\"analysis_py\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Chloride exceedance screening for the Wrack Bay coastal aquifer network.\\n\\nReads the field sample table, scores every grab sample against the 250 mg/L\\nchloride action limit, and tests whether exceedance status is associated with\\nthe shoreline zone in which the sampled well sits.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport csv\\nfrom collections import Counter\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nfrom scipy import stats\\n\\nINPUT_PATH = Path(\\\"data/input.csv\\\")\\nREPORT_PATH = Path(\\\"results/report.md\\\")\\n\\nLIMIT_MG_L = 250.0\\nZONES = (\\\"dune_ridge\\\", \\\"back_barrier\\\", \\\"tidal_flat\\\")\\nPRETTY = {\\n    \\\"dune_ridge\\\": \\\"Dune ridge\\\",\\n    \\\"back_barrier\\\": \\\"Back barrier\\\",\\n    \\\"tidal_flat\\\": \\\"Tidal flat\\\",\\n}\\n\\n\\ndef read_samples(path):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Return the sample rows with their numeric fields converted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    with path.open(newline=\\\"\\\", encoding=\\\"ascii\\\") as handle:\\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(handle))\\n    for row in rows:\\n        row[\\\"visit\\\"] = int(row[\\\"visit\\\"])\\n        row[\\\"depth_m\\\"] = float(row[\\\"depth_m\\\"])\\n        row[\\\"chloride_mg_l\\\"] = float(row[\\\"chloride_mg_l\\\"])\\n    return rows\\n\\n\\ndef contingency(rows):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Zone-by-exceedance counts, one sample row per tallied observation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    counts = np.zeros((len(ZONES), 2), dtype=int)\\n    for row in rows:\\n        zone_ix = ZONES.index(row[\\\"coastal_zone\\\"])\\n        col = 0 if row[\\\"chloride_mg_l\\\"] >= LIMIT_MG_L else 1\\n        counts[zone_ix, col] += 1\\n    return counts\\n\\n\\ndef render(counts, chi2, pval, dof, cramers_v, n_wells, visits):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Build the markdown report text.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    n = int(counts.sum())\\n    rate = {\\n        zone: int(counts[i, 0]) / int(counts[i].sum())\\n        for i, zone in enumerate(ZONES)\\n    }\\n    out = [\\n        \\\"# Chloride exceedance and shoreline zone, Wrack Bay monitoring network\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"## Data\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        f\\\"Source table: data/input.csv ({n} sample rows from {n_wells} monitoring \\\"\\n        f\\\"wells, {visits} visits each).\\\",\\n        \\\"A sample counts as an exceedance when chloride is at or above \\\"\\n        f\\\"{LIMIT_MG_L:.1f} mg/L.\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"| Shoreline zone | Samples | Exceedances | Exceedance rate |\\\",\\n        \\\"| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\\",\\n    ]\\n    for i, zone in enumerate(ZONES):\\n        total = int(counts[i].sum())\\n        hits = int(counts[i, 0])\\n        out.append(f\\\"| {PRETTY[zone]} | {total} | {hits} | {rate[zone]:.3f} |\\\")\\n    out += [\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"## Analysis\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"Pearson chi-squared test of independence (scipy.stats.chi2_contingency) applied\\\",\\n        f\\\"to the {counts.shape[0]} x {counts.shape[1]} table of shoreline zone by \\\"\\n        \\\"exceedance status, with each sample row\\\",\\n        \\\"entered as one observation.\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        f\\\"- chi-squared statistic: {chi2:.4f}\\\",\\n        f\\\"- degrees of freedom: {dof}\\\",\\n        f\\\"- p-value: {pval:.3e}\\\",\\n        f\\\"- Cramer's V: {cramers_v:.3f}\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"## Result\\\",\\n        \\\"\\\",\\n        \\\"[selected-result] Exceedance status is associated with shoreline zone: \\\"\\n        f\\\"Pearson chi-squared test of independence on {n} sample rows gives \\\"\\n        f\\\"chi-squared = {chi2:.4f}, df = {dof}, p = {pval:.3e} \\\"\\n        f\\\"(Cramer's V = {cramers_v:.3f}), with the exceedance rate rising from \\\"\\n        f\\\"{rate['dune_ridge']:.3f} on the dune ridge to \\\"\\n        f\\\"{rate['back_barrier']:.3f} on the back barrier and \\\"\\n        f\\\"{rate['tidal_flat']:.3f} on the tidal flat.\\\",\\n    ]\\n    return \\\"\\\\n\\\".join(out) + \\\"\\\\n\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    rows = read_samples(INPUT_PATH)\\n    counts = contingency(rows)\\n    chi2, pval, dof, _expected = stats.chi2_contingency(counts, correction=False)\\n    total = int(counts.sum())\\n    cramers_v = float(np.sqrt(chi2 / (total * (min(counts.shape) - 1))))\\n    per_well = Counter(row[\\\"well_id\\\"] for row in rows)\\n    report = render(\\n        counts,\\n        chi2,\\n        pval,\\n        dof,\\n        cramers_v,\\n        len(per_well),\\n        max(per_well.values()),\\n    )\\n    REPORT_PATH.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\\n    REPORT_PATH.write_text(report, encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    main()\\n\",\"report_md\":\"# Chloride exceedance and shoreline zone, Wrack Bay monitoring network\\n\\n## Data\\n\\nSource table: data/input.csv (120 sample rows from 30 monitoring wells, 4 visits each).\\nA sample counts as an exceedance when chloride is at or above 250.0 mg/L.\\n\\n| Shoreline zone | Samples | Exceedances | Exceedance rate |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| Dune ridge | 40 | 10 | 0.250 |\\n| Back barrier | 40 | 20 | 0.500 |\\n| Tidal flat | 40 | 30 | 0.750 |\\n\\n## Analysis\\n\\nPearson chi-squared test of independence (scipy.stats.chi2_contingency) applied\\nto the 3 x 2 table of shoreline zone by exceedance status, with each sample row\\nentered as one observation.\\n\\n- chi-squared statistic: 20.0000\\n- degrees of freedom: 2\\n- p-value: 4.540e-05\\n- Cramer's V: 0.408\\n\\n## Result\\n\\n[selected-result] Exceedance status is associated with shoreline zone: Pearson chi-squared test of independence on 120 sample rows gives chi-squared = 20.0000, df = 2, p = 4.540e-05 (Cramer's V = 0.408), with the exceedance rate rising from 0.250 on the dune ridge to 0.500 on the back barrier and 0.750 on the tidal flat.\\n\",\"selected_result_line\":27,\"data_description\":\"# Wrack Bay coastal aquifer chloride monitoring\\n\\nWrack Bay is a barrier-island lagoon whose shallow freshwater lens is watched\\nfor saltwater intrusion. Thirty permanent monitoring wells are screened in the\\nsurficial aquifer, and each well belongs to one of three shoreline zones: the\\ndune ridge farthest from open water, the back-barrier flats behind it, and the\\ntidal flat nearest the inlet. Every well was visited four times during a single\\nfield season. On each visit the well was purged and one grab sample was pumped\\nfrom the screen and sent to the laboratory for chloride analysis. The file\\ntherefore holds 120 sample rows: four rows for each of the thirty wells.\\n\\nColumns:\\n\\n- well_id: identifier of the monitoring well the sample was pumped from. The\\n  same well identifier appears once for each of its four visits, so identifiers\\n  repeat down the file.\\n- coastal_zone: the shoreline zone the well sits in (dune_ridge, back_barrier,\\n  tidal_flat). This is a fixed property of the well, so it is identical across\\n  all four rows belonging to that well.\\n- visit: which of the four scheduled sampling visits produced this row,\\n  numbered 1 through 4.\\n- depth_m: screened depth of the well below ground surface, in metres. Another\\n  fixed well property, repeated on all four of that well's rows.\\n- chloride_mg_l: chloride concentration measured in that visit's grab sample,\\n  in milligrams per litre. The regulatory action limit used by the programme is\\n  250 mg/L.\\n\\nOne row is: one grab sample pumped from one monitoring well on one scheduled visit\\nIndependent unit column: well_id\\n\"}]}","ttft_ms":215278,"ttft_stream_ms":1953,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":263895,"uuid":"75a42919-6c8d-43ad-8658-50cf4e0111ad"}
